. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * 
. 
.         * Model description: Linear regression regressing gender equality att
> itudes as measured in 2018 on having a daughter rather 
.         * than a son as first child with some sociodemographic controls and a
> n indicator on months passed since birth of first child. 
.         * The idea is that having a daughter as a first child is randomly dis
> tributed among parents and uncorrelated with unobserved
.         * characteristics of parents. Excluding multiple births and estimatin
> g robust clustered standard errors at the household level.
. 
.         reg equal_wc_2018_1 i.daughter c.age i.edu i.fam i.gender i.west i.wo
> rk c.msb, vce(cluster hid) 

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =        403
                                                F(10, 258)        =       3.64
                                                Prob > F          =     0.0001
                                                R-squared         =     0.0745
                                                Root MSE          =     1.7928

                                  (Std. err. adjusted for 259 clusters in hid)
